'''Dogenstein''' (名賢わんこ, ''Meiken Wanko'', '''Renowned Doggy''') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[Doge]] introduced in [[Stratospheric Pathway]]. He was added in [[Version 13.2 Update|Version 13.2]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Dogenstein
|image = E 679.png
|first appearance = '''ZL''': [[Permission to Land|Sub-chapter 10 - Permission to Land]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Obvious Cache|Sub-chapter 17 - Obvious Cache]]
|money drop = 250¢ - 987¢
}}

==Enemy==
Dogenstein acts similarly to [[Doge Dark]], but is slightly slower, has [[Area Attack]], doesn't stand still for as long after attacking, and has overall highly improved stats. Combined with his [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] typing, these attributes make it difficult to slow down his progress. He also has a 35% chance to [[Freeze]] Cat Units and a decently fast attack rate, giving him extreme DPS.

Compared to the 150% [[Relic Doge]]s, 600% [[Aku Doge]]s and 200% [[Wild Doge]]s encountered in early Zero Legends, Dogenstein has lower attack power, DPS and speed, but even higher health.

==Strategy==
[[:Category:Sage Slayer Cats|Sage Slayers]] with [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] abilities can be effective, as they can stop Dogestein from moving forth and stopping him from freezing your units (e.g. [[Bowler Cat (Rare Cat)|Bowler Cat]], which has a decent [[Slow]] effect that can almost perma-slow by itself). To counter his Freeze ability, a constant flow of meatshields should negate it, since he only has a meager 120 range. However, it will still be problematic if he reaches your main attackers, as 10,000 base damage and over 8,500 base DPS is still something big to worry about. Use any unit with high damage against Traitless to shred this enemy to pieces.

