==Trivia==
*The word 名賢 ''Meiken'' in Dogenstein's Japanese name (名賢わんこ ''Meiken Wanko'') means renowned, but also sounds just like 名犬, meaning fine dog.
*His design and English name appear to pay homage to the German scientist [[:wikipedia:Albert Einstein|Albert Einstein]]. Though born in Germany, Einstein stayed in the US for the last 22 years of his life, correlating with the American theme of [[Stratospheric Pathway]].
**Dogenstein is the only enemy in [[Heaven-Defying Fruit]] who is not described as a comedian in Japanese. His presence there along with the "Heaven-Defying" in the stage's name and ゆらぎ ''Yuragi'' (Fluctuation) in [[Restricted Area]]'s Japanese name may reference Albert Einstein's quote criticizing quantum fluctuations, "[[wikipedia:Hidden-variable theory#"God does not play dice"|God does not play dice]]".
**His name may also reference the fictional scientist [[wikipedia:Victor Frankenstein|Victor Frankenstein]].

